      "searchText": "Electromagnetic Waves - Topics Home > Electromagnetic Waves Turin Prepnik Electromagnetic Waves In the previous chapter, we assembled the four pillars of Electrodynamics: Maxwell's Equations . Now, we explore their most profound mathematical consequence. In source-free regions, changing fields sustain each other in a self-propagating loop—an Electromagnetic Wave . This chapter traces the path from Maxwell's Equations to the Wave Equation , through the transport of Energy & Momentum , and finally to the behavior of these fields at the boundaries of Matter . Fundamental: Why Waves? Understanding how changing fields sustain each other and why propagation is a physical necessity. → 1. Wave Fundamentals The 1D wave equation, sinusoidal waves, and general properties of oscillations. → 2. EM Waves in Vacuum Deriving wave propagation from Maxwell's Equations, transverse nature, and polarization. → 3. Energy & Momentum The Poynting vector, intensity, and the pressure exerted by light. → 4. Waves in Matter Propagation through dielectrics and conductors, and the physics of boundary conditions. →",
