      "searchText": "Deep Dive: Applications of the Biot-Savart Law Home > Magnetostatics > The Biot-Savart Law > Standard Examples Deep Dive: Applications of the Biot-Savart Law The Biot-Savart law is a universal tool for calculating magnetic fields from steady currents. Below are the detailed derivations for the two most fundamental geometries in magnetostatics. Example 1: The Infinite Straight Wire Problem: Find the magnetic field at a distance $s$ from a long straight wire carrying a steady current $I$. 1. Geometric Setup Let the wire lie along the $z$-axis, carrying current $I$ in the $+\\hat{z}$ direction. We calculate the field at a point $P$ located distance $s$ away on the $x$-axis. Source element: $d\\vec{l}' = dz \\hat{z}$ Separation vector: $\\vecrsep = s \\hat{x} - z \\hat{z}$ Distance: $\\rsep = \\sqrt{s^2 + z^2}$ 2. The Cross Product The Biot-Savart law requires $d\\vec{l}' \\times \\hatrsep$. The magnitude of this cross product is given by $|d\\vec{l}'| \\sin(\\alpha)$, where $\\alpha$ is the angle between the current and the position vector. From geometry, if we define $\\theta$ as the angle from the perpendicular distance $s$, then $\\alpha = 90^\\circ + \\theta$, and $\\sin(90^\\circ + \\theta) = \\cos \\theta$. The direction is circumferential ($\\hat{\\phi}$). $$ dB = \\frac{\\mu_0 I}{4\\pi} \\frac{dz \\cos \\theta}{\\rsep^2} $$ 3. Trigonometric Substitution We express variables $z$ and $r$ in terms of the angle $\\theta$: $$ z = s \\tan \\theta \\implies dz = s \\sec^2 \\theta \\, d\\theta $$ $$ \\rsep = \\frac{s}{\\cos \\theta} $$ Substituting these into the integral: $$ B = \\frac{\\mu_0 I}{4\\pi} \\int \\frac{(s \\sec^2 \\theta \\, d\\theta) \\cos \\theta}{(s / \\cos \\theta)^2} $$ Simplifying the terms: $$ B = \\frac{\\mu_0 I}{4\\pi s} \\int \\cos \\theta \\, d\\theta $$ 4. Integration Limits For an infinite wire ($z \\to \\pm \\inf",
      "snippet": "Deep Dive: Applications of the Biot-Savart Law Home > Magnetostatics > The Biot-Savart Law > Standard Examples Deep Dive: Applications of the Biot-Savart Law The Biot-Savart law is a universal tool for calculating magnet"
